S http://digital.cgdev.org/doc/stata/MO/Misc
N grc1leg2.pkg
D  4 Jun 2024
U 39
d {cmd:grc1leg2}. Add a common legend to combined graphs.
d {cmd:grc1leg2}, like {help graph combine}, arrays separately drawn
d graphs as panels in a single combined graph.  Additionally
d {cmd:grc1leg2} suppresses the legends in the individual graphs
d and adds a common legend borrowed from one of them.
d Options control several characteristics of the common legend
d on the combined graph, including its precise placement.
d Optionally {cmd:grc1leg2} also suppresses the xtitle, the ytitle
d or the main title on the individual graphs and moves one of
d any of these to the combined graph.
d 
d The help file for {cmd:grc1leg2} provides examples of embedding
d a legend in a multi-panel graph, comparing approaches which use,
d respectively, {help graph ..., by()}, {help graph combine} and {cmd:grc1leg2}.
d The dialog offers point-and-click access to {cmd:grc1leg2} options.
d 
d Just as {help graph combine} automatically reduces the size
d of text in component graphs, {cmd:grc1leg2} now automatically
d reduces the size of all elements of the borrowed legend.
d The user can override this default behavior with options
d that control the size of all or individual legend elements.
d 
d Version 2.26 fixes bugs in versions 1.6 and 2.0 - 2.24 that sometimes
d caused {cmd:grc1leg2} to scramble memory graphs and {help serset}s.
d 
d Author: {browse "http://www.cgdev.org/expert/mead-over/":Mead Over}, Center for Global Development
d http://www.cgdev.org/expert/mead-over
d 
d Requires Stata Version 13.1 or later
d 
d Version 2.26 4Nov2023
d Adds ten capabilities to version 1.0.5 of {search grc1leg} 02jun2010, by Vince Wiggins
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20231104
f g\grc1leg2.ado
f g\grc1leg2.sthlp
f g\grc1leg2.dlg
f g\grc1leg2_examples.ado
e
