S http://fmwww.bc.edu/repec/bocode/s
N sspecialreg.pkg
D 17 Oct 2024
U 45
d 'SSPECIALREG': module to estimate binary choice model with discrete endogenous regressor via special regressor method
d 
d  sspecialreg estimates a binary choice model that includes one or
d more endogenous regressors using Lewbel and Dong's special
d regressor method (Econometric Reviews, 2015; Journal of
d Econometrics, 2000). This assumes that the model  includes a
d particular 'special regressor', V, that is exogenous and appears
d additively in the model. It must be continuously distributed with
d a large support. A special regressor with thick tails (greater
d kurtosis) will be more useful as a special regressor.  This
d method has advantages over the linear probability model
d (estimated with OLS or IV), maximum likelihood and control
d function methods. The xtspecialreg command estimates the model in
d a panel data setting, with the data xtset or tsset. The ivreg2 or
d xtivreg2 options, combined with the first option, provide access
d to additional diagnostic tests.
d 
d KW: special regressor
d KW: binary choice
d KW: discrete endogenous regressor
d 
d Requires: Stata version 11 and Jann's kdens from SSC (q.v.)
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20210112
d 
d Author: Christopher F Baum, Boston College
d Support: email baum@@bc.edu
d 
f s\sspecialreg.ado
f s\ssortedfm.ado
f _\_sspecialreg.ado
f s\sspecialreg.sthlp
f x\xtspecialreg.ado
f _\_xtspecialreg.ado
f x\xtspecialreg.sthlp
e
S http://fmwww.bc.edu/repec/bocode/k
N kdens.pkg
D 17 Oct 2024
U 46
d 'KDENS': module for univariate kernel density estimation
d 
d    kdens produces univariate kernel density estimates and graphs
d the result. kdens supplements official Stata's kdensity.
d Important additions are: adaptive (i.e. variable bandwidth)
d kernel density estimation, several automatic bandwidth selectors
d including the Sheather-Jones plug-in estimator, pointwise
d variability bands and confidence intervals, boundary correction
d for variables with bounded domain, fast binned approximation
d estimation. Note that the moremata package, also available from
d SSC, is required.
d 
d KW:  adaptive kernel density
d KW: binned kernel estimator
d KW: Sheather-Jones plug-in
d KW: boundary correction
d KW: reflection
d 
d Requires: Stata version 9.1 and moremata package
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20080526
d 
d Author: Ben Jann, ETH Zurich
d Support: email ben.jann@@soz.gess.ethz.ch
d 
f _\_kdens.ado
f _\_kdens.hlp
f k\kdens.ado
f k\kdens.hlp
f k\kdens.mata
f l\lkdens.mlib
f m\mf_kdens.hlp
f t\twoway_kdens_parse.class
e
S http://fmwww.bc.edu/repec/bocode/r
N rbiprobit.pkg
D 18 Oct 2024
U 47
d 'RBIPROBIT': module to estimate recursive bivariate probit regressions
d 
d  rbiprobit is a user-written command that fits a recursive
d bivariate probit regression using maximum likelihood estimation.
d The model involves an outcome equation and a treatment equation,
d whereas the treatment variable is an endogenous explanatory
d variable of the outcome equation. Both dependent variables have
d to be binary. Postestimation commands allow to compute various
d treatment effects and a decomposition of marginal effects.
d 
d KW: bivariate probit
d KW: recursive
d KW: maximum likelihood
d 
d Requires: Stata version 11
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20220419
d 
d Author: Mustafa Coban, Institute for Employment Research, Nürnberg
d Support: email mustafa.coban@@iab.de
d 
f r\rbiprobit.ado
f r\rbiprobit_lf1.ado
f r\rbiprobit_margdec.ado
f r\rbiprobit_p.ado
f r\rbiprobit_tmeffects.ado
f r\rbiprobit.sthlp
f r\rbiprobit_margdec.sthlp
f r\rbiprobit_postestimation.sthlp
f r\rbiprobit_tmeffects.sthlp
e
S http://fmwww.bc.edu/repec/bocode/s
N sdid.pkg
D 20 Jun 2025
U 48
d 'SDID': module to perform synthetic difference-in-differences estimation, inference, and visualization
d 
d  The sdid command implements the synthetic
d difference-in-differences method of Arkhangelsky et al. (AER,
d 2021) for Stata. The program generates the ATT estimate derived
d in Arkhangelsky et al. (2021), and conducts inference following
d their bootstrap, placebo, or jackknife methods. The command
d allows for multiple treatment dates and multiple treatment units
d directly, as well as cases with only a single treatment unit.  As
d well as estimation and inference, the sdid command includes a
d number of graphical output options to summarize the synthetic
d difference-in-differences estimator.
d 
d KW: difference-in-differences
d KW: DiD
d KW: synthetic
d KW: Arkhangelsky
d 
d Requires: Stata version 13
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20240816
d 
d Author: Daniel Pailañir, Universidad de Santiago de Chile
d Support: email dpailanir@@fen.uchile.cl
d 
d Author: Damian Clarke, Universidad de Santiago de Chile
d Support: email dclarke@@fen.uchile.cl
d 
d Author:  Diego Ciccia, Economics Department, Sciences Po
d Support: email  diego.ciccia@@sciencespo.fr
d 
f s\sdid.ado
f s\sdid.sthlp
e
